00:14:04.206 --> 00:14:06.873
(jets blasting)

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.225
- When she was little, and you
know kids when they're little

00:14:12.225 --> 00:14:13.720
are like, "I'm going to be a singer".

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.293
Or, "I'm going to be an astronaut".

00:14:15.293 --> 00:14:16.793
Did you ever, for one
moment, believe that she

00:14:16.793 --> 00:14:19.543
would grow up to be as
big as she is right now?

00:14:19.543 --> 00:14:23.601
- Actually, as a child, she was
very childish to begin with,

00:14:23.601 --> 00:14:25.501
(laughing)

00:14:25.501 --> 00:14:29.404
- [Host] As a child, a very
childish child, actually.

00:14:29.404 --> 00:14:32.746
- But she was very determined, alright?

00:14:32.746 --> 00:14:37.242
And we could see it in her
when she was four, you know--

00:14:37.242 --> 00:14:38.822
- Oh I'm so embarrassed.

00:14:38.822 --> 00:14:40.064
- She would stand in front of the piano

00:14:40.064 --> 00:14:41.816
and just bang on the keys, and then

00:14:41.816 --> 00:14:43.899
she wrote her first song,

00:14:44.797 --> 00:14:47.880
I used to play "Money" by Pink Floyd,

00:14:48.908 --> 00:14:50.198
and she wrote her first song,

00:14:50.198 --> 00:14:52.459
it was called "Dollar Bill".

00:14:52.459 --> 00:14:53.292
- [Host] I love that.

00:14:53.292 --> 00:14:55.407
And Cynthia, my wife, she still has it.

00:14:55.407 --> 00:14:56.963
- We should have that.

00:14:56.963 --> 00:14:58.601
- Yeah, well. (laughter)

00:14:58.601 --> 00:15:00.569
- It was because, you know,
on that record they use,

00:15:00.569 --> 00:15:04.736
they use actual money, and
the register as instruments,

00:15:05.686 --> 00:15:08.659
and I remember as a kid I
was so fascinated by that.

00:15:08.659 --> 00:15:11.030
So my dad played me a lot of great music

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.933
that made me really fall in love

00:15:12.933 --> 00:15:15.212
with that idea of making it.

00:15:15.212 --> 00:15:19.379
My greatest influence in
this house, for ten years,

00:15:21.688 --> 00:15:24.155
was Whitney.
- Really?

00:15:24.155 --> 00:15:28.085
- Yes. And I used to stand
at the top of that staircase,

00:15:28.085 --> 00:15:31.047
and sing "The Star Spangled Banner"

00:15:31.047 --> 00:15:33.393
every single day after school.

00:15:33.393 --> 00:15:38.230
I would play it over and
over and I would study--

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.800
- Her version of "The
Star Spangled Banner".

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:44.967
- And I used to stand up
there, and I would study her,

00:15:46.514 --> 00:15:49.079
it's so interesting that
you brought that up, Mom.

00:15:49.079 --> 00:15:50.882
It's like, I don't forget about it,

00:15:50.882 --> 00:15:54.218
but I thanked her at the
Grammy's when I won that award,

00:15:54.218 --> 00:15:58.301
because she, for me, is
the greatest of all time.

00:15:59.237 --> 00:16:00.070
- Really?

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:01.725
- The greatest of all time.

00:16:01.725 --> 00:16:05.915
I need to say thank you
tonight to Whitney Houston.

00:16:05.915 --> 00:16:08.257
I wanted to thank Whitney because,

00:16:08.257 --> 00:16:11.743
when I wrote "Born This Way",
I imagined she was singing it,

00:16:11.743 --> 00:16:14.133
because I wasn't secure enough in myself

00:16:14.133 --> 00:16:17.428
to imagine I was a superstar, so Whitney,

00:16:17.428 --> 00:16:20.249
I imagined you were singing
"Born This Way" when I wrote it,

00:16:20.249 --> 00:16:21.371
thank you.

00:16:21.371 --> 00:16:22.907
- Will you look under the rock,

00:16:22.907 --> 00:16:24.583
and will you search for
tweets, and search for

00:16:24.583 --> 00:16:26.318
comments and see what people are saying?

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:29.744
- Well, you know, I like to
stay in contact with the fans,

00:16:29.744 --> 00:16:33.981
and I want to see how they're
doing and enjoying the music,

00:16:33.981 --> 00:16:38.292
and pick up on their
little artistic nuances,

00:16:38.292 --> 00:16:40.767
the things that they
create and that they say,

00:16:40.767 --> 00:16:43.725
but, I'm just in a
different place in my life

00:16:43.725 --> 00:16:46.944
I don't allow things that are
negative to run everything.

00:16:46.944 --> 00:16:51.755
I think it's important to
just try to stay grounded

00:16:51.755 --> 00:16:55.473
in who you are, and the
things that come your way

00:16:55.473 --> 00:16:56.659
just be grateful for them.

